/-!
# Positive-rank Fitting-action recognition in G.9.4

The five outputs retain the concrete groups, the literal normal closure,
and the marked natural actions. The nilpotent covering-group input is proved
from B.5.2, and the plane branch is recognized as the full binary linear
group and hence S₃. Given the independent three-core reduction, the degree
case theorem leaves precisely the degree-four and degree-six branches.

The noncubic Fitting branch, the three-core reduction, and the GL₄/GL₆
normalizer and overgroup recognition are still required for the full
conditional G.9.4 implication. No theorem here asserts that implication.
The positive-rank convention is explicit; the original `FittingHypothesis`
and the rank-zero diagnostic in `Obstructions` are unchanged.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, G.9.4, printed pp.354--355, PDF pp.365--366.
-/
